    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but some of the council members are saying that \"transitioning toward sustainable solutions\" is just a fancy way of saying we're going to ignore the needs of people who can't afford rail or don't live near it. it feels like a heavy bias toward urban centers. do you think it's actually possible to have a plan that doesn't basically treat car-dependency as something that just needs to be phased out?",
